  "modification_plan": "1. gn_stats_kernel -> vectorized: keep grid (nchunk,B), block 256. Map tid: cq = tid & 63 (channel quad, channels 4*cq..4*cq+3), pl = tid >> 6 (0..3). Replace the 4 scalar loads with `float4 v = *reinterpret_cast<const float4*>(x + ((long)b*HW + p)*256 + 4*cq);` and loop `for (p = pstart+pl; p < pend; p += 4)`. Accumulate s += (v.x+v.y)+(v.z+v.w); s2 += (v.x*v.x+v.y*v.y)+(v.z*v.z+v.w*v.w). Since 8 channels/group and 4|8, the quad is group-pure. Reduce group: `__shfl_down_sync(0xffffffff,s,1,2)` (pairs cq even/odd = one group), then combine the 4 pl partials through `__shared__ float sp[2][4][32]` and have the 32 threads with pl==0,cq even sum 4 values and write part[]/part[sq_off+..] exactly as today.\n2. gn_apply_silu_kernel -> vectorized: same tid mapping (cq, pl); precompute float4 sc/sh once per thread from gamma/beta/mean/rstd with g = cq>>1; each block covers 32 positions (grid.x = (HW+31)/32); inner `#pragma unroll 8` loop over pl+4*i: one float4 load, 4 FMAs, 4 SiLUs, one float4 store. Tail guarded by scalar path when p >= HW.\n3. gn_apply_silu_res_nchw_kernel (hottest): keep TP=64/TC=64 tile, change smem row pitch to `sm[cl*(TP+4)+pl]` (68 floats = 272B, 16B aligned; 17.4KB/block, under the 99KB/block limit and equal to today's footprint so occupancy is unchanged). Phase 1: each thread loads one float4 of 4 channels for one p (`x + ((b*HW+p)*256) + c0 + 4*cq`), applies sc/sh + SiLU on the 4 lanes, writes 4 scalars into 4 smem rows. Phase 2: each thread owns one cl and 4 consecutive pl -> one 16B smem load, one float4 residual load from `res + (b*CH+c0+cl)*HW + p`, one float4 store to `out + same`. This replaces 4 scalar global loads+4 stores per thread with 1+1+1 vector ops.\n4. nchw2nhwc_kernel -> vectorized: phase 1 reads float4 along p (contiguous NCHW) into smem with pitch (TP+4); phase 2 gathers 4 channels from smem (4 scalar smem reads, stride 68 floats) and issues ONE 16B global store per thread to NHWC. Global traffic becomes fully 128-bit in both directions.\n5. Alignment/shape guard in fused_block: use the vectorized kernels only when (HW % 4 == 0) && all data_ptrs 16B aligned (true for at::empty) && C == 256; otherwise launch the existing scalar kernels verbatim (keeps 2x256x64x64 and any odd shape safe).\n6. Do not change: launch counts, conv calls, weight packing, gn_finalize, stream usage, tensor layouts/allocations, output NCHW format. Grid sizes must still give >= 2 waves/SM (mid: stats 2048 blocks, apply 4096, transpose 4096 -> ok).\n7. Keep registers <= 48/thread (check with -Xptxas -v); if the vectorized apply kernel spills, drop the unroll from 8 to 4.\n8. Numerics: identical fp32 FMA/SiLU expressions; only the stats summation order changes (still hierarchical fp32), well inside max_atol 0.0028.",
  "evidence": "gn_apply_silu_res_nchw_kernel 114.75us at gpu__dram_throughput 88.81% and sm__throughput 19.41%, long_scoreboard 68.77%; gn_apply_silu_kernel 74.9us with long_scoreboard 91.96% and SM SOL 12.85%; gn_stats_kernel moves 67.1MB in 45.8us = 1.465 TB/s vs the 1.79 TB/s that gn_apply reaches, i.e. 
