  "bottleneck": "[DRAM-latency-bound, memory-instruction-limited] Hottest non-removable kernel gn_apply_silu_res_nchw_kernel (114.75us, 88.8% DRAM SOL but only 19.4% SM SOL, 68.8% long-scoreboard stall). It and the other three custom kernels (359us total) stream with scalar 4-byte accesses, so each warp keeps only 128B in flight per instruction and none reaches the ~1.765 TB/s achievable DRAM rate (85.7-89.0%).",
